                <head>248. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Queen Frederika of Greece visited the United States October 21–December 14. Her
                    visit was an informal one primarily concerned with studying the U.S. atomic
                    energy program. The Queen was in Washington October 22–25 for discussions with
                    Department of State officials and on December 9 for a meeting with President
                    Eisenhower. No records of her talks with Department of State officials have been
                    found. In an October 30 letter, Rountree reported to Riddleberger that
                    discussions with the Queen centered on the Cyprus question. (Department of
                    State, Greek Desk Files: Lot 61 D 1, Athens Embassy) During her December 9
                    meeting with Eisenhower, the Queen discussed prospects for world peace and
                    disarmament. A memorandum of this conversation is in the Eisenhower Library,
                    Whitman File, DDE Diaries.</p>
            </div>
